From a80a8b1a77fd5d71c1c3f2c84c20da1b8f964ffe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@buttzeppelin>
Date: Fri, 20 Feb 2026 12:08:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: Increment unlootedCount for AoE-merged loot items
 (I-137)

Items merged from nearby corpses into the main creature's loot were not
incrementing unlootedCount, causing uint8 underflow when looted. This
made isLooted() permanently false, preventing AllLootRemovedFromCorpse()
from firing and the skinnable flag from being set.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/aoe_loot.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/aoe_loot.cpp b/src/aoe_loot.cpp
index fd092fd..d5fb9b8 100644
--- a/src/aoe_loot.cpp
+++ b/src/aoe_loot.cpp
@@ -177,7 +177,11 @@ bool AOELootServer::CanPacketReceive(WorldSession* session, WorldPacket& packet)
     for (const auto& item : itemsToAdd)
     {
         if (mainLoot->items.size() < 15)
+        {
             mainLoot->items.push_back(item);
+            if (!item.is_looted)
+                ++mainLoot->unlootedCount;
+        }
     }
 
     // Add quest items to player inventory
